            <ArticleTitle>Two-dimensional stress echocardiography in coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>403-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Stress echocardiography done using various methods has become a primary way to assess and quantify the extent of myocardial ischemia. Although it is highly versatile, its use remains patchy, and in many centers it is simply considered a research technique. This review discusses some of the advantages of stress echocardiography in relation to recent publications, and it points to some areas for future research.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
